-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 10, Contempts of the lawful authority of
-- public servants (ss 172-190). Part of the state-public group (Chapters 6-10).
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026 (inputs/PC1871.txt). Each section's text is quoted above its rules.
--
-- GENERATED by notes/state-public-gen/build.py from the hand-written ladders in
-- notes/state-public-gen/part_contempts.py; edit there and rebuild.
--
-- The charge-generator contract (BRIEF.md, notes/PLAN.md sections 3, 6, 8): one facts
-- record per section family, taken as `GIVEN f`; the defining predicate; one
-- `offence under s N` per punishing provision; one `charge under s N` returning
-- a `Charge`. Most sections here punish in two paragraphs - (a) "in the case of
-- an individual", (b) "in any other case" - which differ only in punishment, so
-- the leaf `the accused is an individual` chooses the punishment and the
-- paragraph the charge cites ("186(1)(a)"), never whether it is made out.
-- Where a subsection (2) adds an element (a court, an offence), it is its own
-- `offence under s N(2)` over the same record, and calls `offence under s N(1)`.
--
-- "public servant" is a flat leaf (PLAN section 3.3); s 21(2) narrows it for
-- ss 175, 178, 179 and 180, and those leaves say so.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-state-public-common`

§ `Chapter 10 - Contempts of the lawful authority of public servants`

§§ `s 172 - Absconding to avoid arrest on warrant or service of summons, etc., proceeding from a public servant`

--   172. Whoever absconds in order to avoid being arrested on a warrant, or to
--   avoid being served with a summons, a notice, or an order proceeding from any
--   public servant, legally competent, as such public servant, to issue such
--   warrant, summons, notice or order, shall be punished with imprisonment for a
--   term which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500,
--   or with both; or, if the summons, notice or order is to attend in person or
--   by agent, or to produce a document or an electronic record before a court of
--   justice, with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with
--   fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 172
DECLARE `Absconding Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    absconds
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused abscond - leave or hide from the place where they could be found?
    `in order to avoid being arrested on a warrant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in order to avoid being arrested on a warrant?
    `in order to avoid being served with a summons, a notice or an order`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in order to avoid being served with a summons, a notice or an order?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `legally competent, as such public servant, to issue such warrant, summons, notice or order`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the public servant from whom it proceeded legally competent, as such, to issue it?
    `the summons, notice or order is to attend in person or by agent, or to produce a document or an electronic record, before a court of justice`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the summons, notice or order one to attend in person or by agent, or to produce a document or electronic record, before a court of justice (s 20)? This chooses the higher punishment; it is not an element.
    `the process`
        IS A STRING @desc The warrant, summons, notice or order, as it is to read in the charge - for example "a warrant of arrest issued by the State Courts on 3 March 2026"
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 172
`punishment prescribed by s 172` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "172"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 1
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 172
`punishment prescribed by s 172, where the summons, notice or order is to attend or produce before a court of justice` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "172"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused absconds to avoid arrest on a warrant or service of a summons, notice or order, within section 172 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS AN `Absconding Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `absconds to avoid arrest or service` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's absconds
    AND (    f's `in order to avoid being arrested on a warrant`
         OR  f's `in order to avoid being served with a summons, a notice or an order` )
    AND "proceeding from any"
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `legally competent, as such public servant, to issue such warrant, summons, notice or order`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 172 of the Penal Code 1871 (absconding to avoid arrest or service)
GIVEN f IS AN `Absconding Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 172` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `absconds to avoid arrest or service` f

@export Frame a charge under section 172 of the Penal Code 1871 (absconding to avoid arrest on a warrant or service of a summons, notice or order), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Absconding Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 172` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "172" "absconding to avoid arrest on a warrant or service of a summons, notice or order"
        (IF f's `the summons, notice or order is to attend in person or by agent, or to produce a document or an electronic record, before a court of justice` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 172, where the summons, notice or order is to attend or produce before a court of justice`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 172`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 172` f)
        (CONCAT "did abscond in order to avoid ", (IF f's `in order to avoid being arrested on a warrant` THEN "being arrested on " ELSE "being served with "), f's `the process`, ", proceeding from ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant legally competent to issue the same", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's absconds) "absconds"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `in order to avoid being arrested on a warrant` OR f's `in order to avoid being served with a summons, a notice or an order`) "in order to avoid being arrested on a warrant, or being served with a summons, a notice or an order"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "proceeding from a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally competent, as such public servant, to issue such warrant, summons, notice or order`) "legally competent, as such public servant, to issue it"),
            (`missing unless` (`absconds to avoid arrest or service` f) "the elements of section 172 taken together")))

§§ `s 173 - Preventing service of summons, etc., or preventing publication thereof`

--   173.-(1) A person who in any manner -
--
--   (a) intentionally prevents the serving on himself, or on any other person,
--   of any summons, notice or order, proceeding from any public servant legally
--   competent, as such public servant, to issue such summons, notice or order;
--
--   (b) intentionally prevents the lawful affixing to any place of any such
--   summons, notice or order, or intentionally removes any such summons, notice
--   or order from any place to which it is lawfully affixed; or
--
--   (c) intentionally prevents the lawful making of any proclamation, under the
--   authority of any public servant legally competent, as such public servant,
--   to direct such proclamation to be made, shall -
--
--   (d) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (e) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.
--
--   (2) If the summons, notice, order, or proclamation is to attend in person or
--   by agent before a court, or to produce a document or an electronic record
--   before a court, any person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)
--   shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 173
DECLARE `Preventing Service Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the accused is an individual`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused an individual (a human being)? Paragraph (a) of the punishment applies to an individual; paragraph (b), "in any other case", to a company, association or body of persons (s 11). This leaf chooses the punishment, not whether the offence is made out.
    intentionally
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act intentionally (s 26C)?
    `prevents the serving on himself, or on any other person, of any summons, notice or order`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Did the accused, in any manner, prevent the serving of a summons, notice or order on themselves or on anyone else?
    `prevents the lawful affixing to any place of any such summons, notice or order`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Did the accused prevent the lawful affixing of such a summons, notice or order to any place?
    `removes any such summons, notice or order from any place to which it is lawfully affixed`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Did the accused remove such a summons, notice or order from a place to which it was lawfully affixed?
    `prevents the lawful making of any proclamation`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Did the accused prevent the lawful making of a proclamation?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `legally competent, as such public servant, to issue such summons, notice or order, or to direct such proclamation to be made`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the public servant from whom the summons, notice or order proceeded (or under whose authority the proclamation was made) legally competent, as such, to issue it or direct it?
    `the summons, notice, order or proclamation is to attend in person or by agent before a court, or to produce a document or an electronic record before a court`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (2) Is the summons, notice, order or proclamation one to attend in person or by agent before a court, or to produce a document or electronic record before a court?
    `the process`
        IS A STRING @desc The summons, notice, order or proclamation, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 173(1)(d)
`punishment prescribed by s 173(1)(d)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "173(1)(d)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 1
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 173(1)(e)
`punishment prescribed by s 173(1)(e)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "173(1)(e)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 173(2)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 173(2)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "173(2)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 173(2)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 173(2)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "173(2)(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused prevents the service, affixing or proclamation of a summons, notice, order or proclamation within section 173(1) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Preventing Service Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `prevents service or publication` f IF
        "(1) A person who in any manner -"
    AND f's intentionally
    AND (    f's `prevents the serving on himself, or on any other person, of any summons, notice or order`
         OR  f's `prevents the lawful affixing to any place of any such summons, notice or order`
         OR  f's `removes any such summons, notice or order from any place to which it is lawfully affixed`
         OR  f's `prevents the lawful making of any proclamation` )
    AND "proceeding from, or under the authority of, any"
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `legally competent, as such public servant, to issue such summons, notice or order, or to direct such proclamation to be made`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 173(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (preventing service of a summons, etc.)
GIVEN f IS A `Preventing Service Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 173(1)` f IF
        "A person who"
    ... `prevents service or publication` f

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence under section 173(1) of the Penal Code 1871 that section 173(2) punishes more severely (the summons, etc. is to attend or produce before a court)
GIVEN f IS A `Preventing Service Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 173(2)` f IF
        "any person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)"
    AND `offence under s 173(1)` f
    AND "(2) If"
    AND f's `the summons, notice, order or proclamation is to attend in person or by agent before a court, or to produce a document or an electronic record before a court`

@export Frame a charge under section 173(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (preventing the service of a summons, notice or order, or the making of a proclamation), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Preventing Service Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 173(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "173(1)(d)" ELSE "173(1)(e)") "preventing the service of a summons, notice or order, or the making of a proclamation"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 173(1)(d)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 173(1)(e)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 173(1)` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally prevent ", `joined with` ", or " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's `prevents the serving on himself, or on any other person, of any summons, notice or order`) "the serving"), (`included if` (f's `prevents the lawful affixing to any place of any such summons, notice or order`) "the lawful affixing"), (`included if` (f's `prevents the lawful making of any proclamation`) "the lawful making"))), " of ", f's `the process`, ", proceeding from ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant legally competent to issue the same", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `prevents the serving on himself, or on any other person, of any summons, notice or order` OR f's `prevents the lawful affixing to any place of any such summons, notice or order` OR f's `removes any such summons, notice or order from any place to which it is lawfully affixed` OR f's `prevents the lawful making of any proclamation`) "prevents the serving, the lawful affixing or the lawful making of the summons, notice, order or proclamation, or removes it"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "proceeding from a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally competent, as such public servant, to issue such summons, notice or order, or to direct such proclamation to be made`) "legally competent, as such public servant, to issue or direct it"),
            (`missing unless` (`prevents service or publication` f) "the elements of section 173(1) taken together")))

@export Frame a charge under section 173(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (preventing the service of a summons, notice or order to attend or produce before a court), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Preventing Service Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 173(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "173(2)(a)" ELSE "173(2)(b)") "preventing the service of a summons, notice or order to attend or produce before a court"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 173(2)(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 173(2)(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 173(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally prevent ", `joined with` ", or " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's `prevents the serving on himself, or on any other person, of any summons, notice or order`) "the serving"), (`included if` (f's `prevents the lawful affixing to any place of any such summons, notice or order`) "the lawful affixing"), (`included if` (f's `prevents the lawful making of any proclamation`) "the lawful making"))), " of ", f's `the process`, ", proceeding from ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant legally competent to issue the same", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `prevents the serving on himself, or on any other person, of any summons, notice or order` OR f's `prevents the lawful affixing to any place of any such summons, notice or order` OR f's `removes any such summons, notice or order from any place to which it is lawfully affixed` OR f's `prevents the lawful making of any proclamation`) "prevents the serving, the lawful affixing or the lawful making of the summons, notice, order or proclamation, or removes it"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "proceeding from a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally competent, as such public servant, to issue such summons, notice or order, or to direct such proclamation to be made`) "legally competent, as such public servant, to issue or direct it"),
            (`missing unless` (`prevents service or publication` f) "the elements of section 173(1) taken together"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `the summons, notice, order or proclamation is to attend in person or by agent before a court, or to produce a document or an electronic record before a court`) "the summons, notice, order or proclamation is to attend or to produce a document or electronic record before a court")))

§§ `s 174 - Failure to attend in obedience to order from public servant`

--   174.-(1) A person who, being legally bound to attend in person or by an
--   agent at a certain place and time in obedience to a summons, a notice, an
--   order or a proclamation, proceeding from any public servant legally
--   competent, as such public servant, to issue the same, intentionally omits to
--   attend at the place or time, or departs from the place where the person is
--   bound to attend before the time at which it is lawful for the person to
--   depart, shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.
--
--   (2) If the summons, notice, order or proclamation is to attend in person or
--   by agent before a court, any person who is guilty of an offence under
--   subsection (1) shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.
--
--   Illustrations
--
--   (a) A, being legally bound to appear before the General Division of the High
--   Court, in obedience to an order to attend court issuing from the General
--   Division of the High Court, intentionally omits to appear. A has committed
--   the offence defined in this section.
--
--   (b) A, being legally bound to appear before a Magistrate as a witness, in
--   obedience to a summons issued by that Magistrate, intentionally omits to
--   appear. A has committed the offence defined in this section.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 174
DECLARE `Failure to Attend Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the accused is an individual`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused an individual (a human being)? Paragraph (a) of the punishment applies to an individual; paragraph (b), "in any other case", to a company, association or body of persons (s 11). This leaf chooses the punishment, not whether the offence is made out.
    `legally bound to attend in person or by an agent at a certain place and time`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused legally bound to attend, in person or by an agent, at a certain place and time?
    `in obedience to a summons, a notice, an order or a proclamation`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that obligation one of obedience to a summons, a notice, an order or a proclamation?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `legally competent, as such public servant, to issue the same`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the public servant from whom it proceeded legally competent, as such, to issue it?
    intentionally
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act intentionally (s 26C)?
    `omits to attend at the place or time`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused fail to attend at the place or at the time?
    `departs from the place before the time at which it is lawful to depart`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused leave the place before the time at which it was lawful to leave?
    `the summons, notice, order or proclamation is to attend in person or by agent before a court`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (2) Is the summons, notice, order or proclamation one to attend in person or by agent before a court?
    `the process`
        IS A STRING @desc The summons, notice, order or proclamation, as it is to read in the charge - for example "a summons issued by a Magistrate to attend Court 4A of the State Courts at 9.00 am on 5 May 2026"
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 174(1)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 174(1)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "174(1)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 1
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 174(1)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 174(1)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "174(1)(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 174(2)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 174(2)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "174(2)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 174(2)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 174(2)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "174(2)(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
