    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused fails to attend in obedience to a summons, notice, order or proclamation within section 174(1) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Failure to Attend Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fails to attend in obedience to an order from a public servant` f IF
        "(1) A person who, being"
    AND f's `legally bound to attend in person or by an agent at a certain place and time`
    AND f's `in obedience to a summons, a notice, an order or a proclamation`
    AND "proceeding from any"
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `legally competent, as such public servant, to issue the same`
    AND f's intentionally
    AND (    f's `omits to attend at the place or time`
         OR  f's `departs from the place before the time at which it is lawful to depart` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 174(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (failure to attend in obedience to an order from a public servant)
GIVEN f IS A `Failure to Attend Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 174(1)` f IF
        "A person who"
    ... `fails to attend in obedience to an order from a public servant` f

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence under section 174(1) of the Penal Code 1871 that section 174(2) punishes more severely (the order is to attend before a court)
GIVEN f IS A `Failure to Attend Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 174(2)` f IF
        "any person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)"
    AND `offence under s 174(1)` f
    AND "(2) If"
    AND f's `the summons, notice, order or proclamation is to attend in person or by agent before a court`

@export Frame a charge under section 174(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (failure to attend in obedience to an order from a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Failure to Attend Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 174(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "174(1)(a)" ELSE "174(1)(b)") "failure to attend in obedience to an order from a public servant"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 174(1)(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 174(1)(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 174(1)` f)
        (CONCAT "being legally bound to attend in obedience to ", f's `the process`, ", proceeding from ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant legally competent to issue the same, did intentionally ", (IF f's `omits to attend at the place or time` THEN "omit to attend at the place and time stated therein" ELSE "depart from the place before the time at which it was lawful to depart"), `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound to attend in person or by an agent at a certain place and time`) "legally bound to attend in person or by an agent at a certain place and time"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `in obedience to a summons, a notice, an order or a proclamation`) "in obedience to a summons, a notice, an order or a proclamation"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "proceeding from a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally competent, as such public servant, to issue the same`) "legally competent, as such public servant, to issue the same"),
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `omits to attend at the place or time` OR f's `departs from the place before the time at which it is lawful to depart`) "omits to attend at the place or time, or departs before the time at which it is lawful to depart"),
            (`missing unless` (`fails to attend in obedience to an order from a public servant` f) "the elements of section 174(1) taken together")))

@export Frame a charge under section 174(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (failure to attend court in obedience to an order from a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Failure to Attend Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 174(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "174(2)(a)" ELSE "174(2)(b)") "failure to attend court in obedience to an order from a public servant"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 174(2)(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 174(2)(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 174(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "being legally bound to attend in obedience to ", f's `the process`, ", proceeding from ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant legally competent to issue the same, did intentionally ", (IF f's `omits to attend at the place or time` THEN "omit to attend at the place and time stated therein" ELSE "depart from the place before the time at which it was lawful to depart"), `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound to attend in person or by an agent at a certain place and time`) "legally bound to attend in person or by an agent at a certain place and time"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `in obedience to a summons, a notice, an order or a proclamation`) "in obedience to a summons, a notice, an order or a proclamation"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "proceeding from a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally competent, as such public servant, to issue the same`) "legally competent, as such public servant, to issue the same"),
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `omits to attend at the place or time` OR f's `departs from the place before the time at which it is lawful to depart`) "omits to attend at the place or time, or departs before the time at which it is lawful to depart"),
            (`missing unless` (`fails to attend in obedience to an order from a public servant` f) "the elements of section 174(1) taken together"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `the summons, notice, order or proclamation is to attend in person or by agent before a court`) "the summons, notice, order or proclamation is to attend in person or by agent before a court")))

§§ `s 175 - Omission to produce document or electronic record to public servant by person legally bound to produce such document or electronic record`

--   175. A person who, being legally bound to produce or deliver up any document
--   or electronic record to any public servant, as such, intentionally omits so
--   to produce or deliver up the same, shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 175; s 21(2)
DECLARE `Omission to Produce Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the accused is an individual`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused an individual (a human being)? Paragraph (a) of the punishment applies to an individual; paragraph (b), "in any other case", to a company, association or body of persons (s 11). This leaf chooses the punishment, not whether the offence is made out.
    `legally bound to produce or deliver up any document or electronic record`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused legally bound (s 43) to produce or deliver up a document (s 29) or an electronic record (s 29B)?
    `to any public servant, as such`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the obligation owed to a public servant in that capacity?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21, read with section 21(2): for this section a judge as defined in the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016 is NOT a public servant? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21, for sections 175, 178, 179, 180 and 228`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    intentionally
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act intentionally (s 26C)?
    `omits so to produce or deliver up the same`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused fail to produce or deliver it up?
    `the document`
        IS A STRING @desc The document or electronic record, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 175(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 175(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "175(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 1
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 175(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 175(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "175(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused, legally bound to produce a document or electronic record to a public servant, intentionally omits to, within section 175 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Produce Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `omits to produce a document to a public servant` f IF
        "A person who, being"
    AND f's `legally bound to produce or deliver up any document or electronic record`
    AND f's `to any public servant, as such`
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's intentionally
    AND f's `omits so to produce or deliver up the same`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 175 of the Penal Code 1871 (omission to produce a document to a public servant)
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Produce Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 175` f IF
        "A person who"
    ... `omits to produce a document to a public servant` f

@export Frame a charge under section 175 of the Penal Code 1871 (omission to produce a document or electronic record to a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Produce Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 175` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "175(a)" ELSE "175(b)") "omission to produce a document or electronic record to a public servant"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 175(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 175(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 175` f)
        (CONCAT "being legally bound to produce ", f's `the document`, " to ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, did intentionally omit to produce the same", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound to produce or deliver up any document or electronic record`) "legally bound to produce or deliver up a document or electronic record"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `to any public servant, as such` AND f's `public servant`) "to a public servant, as such"),
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `omits so to produce or deliver up the same`) "omits so to produce or deliver up the same"),
            (`missing unless` (`omits to produce a document to a public servant` f) "the elements of section 175 taken together")))

§§ `s 176 - Omission to give notice or information to public servant by person legally bound to give such notice or information`

--   176.-(1) A person who, being legally bound to give any notice or to furnish
--   information on any subject to any public servant, as such, intentionally
--   omits to give such notice or to furnish such information in the manner and
--   at the time required by law, shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.
--
--   (2) If the notice or information required to be given respects the
--   commission of an offence, or is required for the purpose of preventing the
--   commission of an offence or in order to the apprehension of an offender, any
--   person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 176; s 177 Explanation; s 40(3)
DECLARE `Omission to Inform Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the accused is an individual`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused an individual (a human being)? Paragraph (a) of the punishment applies to an individual; paragraph (b), "in any other case", to a company, association or body of persons (s 11). This leaf chooses the punishment, not whether the offence is made out.
    `legally bound to give any notice or to furnish information on any subject`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused legally bound (s 43) to give a notice, or to furnish information on some subject?
    `to any public servant, as such`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the obligation owed to a public servant in that capacity?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    intentionally
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act intentionally (s 26C)?
    `omits to give such notice or to furnish such information in the manner and at the time required by law`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused fail to give the notice or furnish the information in the manner and at the time the law required?
    `the notice or information respects the commission of an offence, or is required for the purpose of preventing the commission of an offence or in order to the apprehension of an offender`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (2) Does the notice or information concern the commission of an offence, or is it required to prevent an offence or to apprehend an offender? By the Explanation to s 177, "offence" here includes an act outside Singapore that would be punishable in Singapore under s 302, 304, 382, 392-397, 399, 402, 435, 436, 449, 450, 459 or 460, and "offender" anyone alleged to have done one. By s 40(3), "offence" also covers another law's offence punishable with 6 months' imprisonment or more.
    `the notice or information`
        IS A STRING @desc The notice or information, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 176(1)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 176(1)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "176(1)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 1
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 176(1)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 176(1)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "176(1)(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 176(2)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 176(2)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "176(2)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 176(2)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 176(2)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "176(2)(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused, legally bound to give notice or information to a public servant, intentionally omits to, within section 176(1) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Inform Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `omits to give notice or information to a public servant` f IF
        "(1) A person who, being"
    AND f's `legally bound to give any notice or to furnish information on any subject`
    AND f's `to any public servant, as such`
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's intentionally
    AND f's `omits to give such notice or to furnish such information in the manner and at the time required by law`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 176(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (omission to give notice or information to a public servant)
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Inform Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 176(1)` f IF
        "A person who"
    ... `omits to give notice or information to a public servant` f

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence under section 176(1) of the Penal Code 1871 that section 176(2) punishes more severely (the information concerns an offence)
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Inform Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 176(2)` f IF
        "any person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)"
    AND `offence under s 176(1)` f
    AND "(2) If"
    AND f's `the notice or information respects the commission of an offence, or is required for the purpose of preventing the commission of an offence or in order to the apprehension of an offender`

@export Frame a charge under section 176(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (omission to give notice or information to a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Inform Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 176(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "176(1)(a)" ELSE "176(1)(b)") "omission to give notice or information to a public servant"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 176(1)(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 176(1)(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 176(1)` f)
        (CONCAT "being legally bound to give ", f's `the notice or information`, " to ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, did intentionally omit to give the same in the manner and at the time required by law", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound to give any notice or to furnish information on any subject`) "legally bound to give a notice or to furnish information"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `to any public servant, as such` AND f's `public servant`) "to a public servant, as such"),
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `omits to give such notice or to furnish such information in the manner and at the time required by law`) "omits to give it in the manner and at the time required by law"),
            (`missing unless` (`omits to give notice or information to a public servant` f) "the elements of section 176(1) taken together")))

@export Frame a charge under section 176(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (omission to give information to a public servant respecting an offence), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Inform Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 176(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "176(2)(a)" ELSE "176(2)(b)") "omission to give information to a public servant respecting an offence"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 176(2)(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 176(2)(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 176(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "being legally bound to give ", f's `the notice or information`, " to ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, did intentionally omit to give the same in the manner and at the time required by law", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound to give any notice or to furnish information on any subject`) "legally bound to give a notice or to furnish information"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `to any public servant, as such` AND f's `public servant`) "to a public servant, as such"),
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `omits to give such notice or to furnish such information in the manner and at the time required by law`) "omits to give it in the manner and at the time required by law"),
            (`missing unless` (`omits to give notice or information to a public servant` f) "the elements of section 176(1) taken together"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `the notice or information respects the commission of an offence, or is required for the purpose of preventing the commission of an offence or in order to the apprehension of an offender`) "the notice or information respects the commission of an offence, or is required to prevent one or to apprehend an offender")))

§§ `s 177 - Furnishing false information`

--   177.-(1) A person who, being legally bound to furnish information on any
--   subject to any public servant, as such, furnishes, as true, information on
--   the subject which the person knows or has reason to believe to be false,
--   shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.
--
--   (2) If the information which the person mentioned in subsection (1) is
--   legally bound to furnish respects the commission of an offence, or is
--   required for the purpose of preventing the commission of an offence, or in
--   order to the apprehension of an offender, the person who is guilty of an
--   offence under that subsection shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine.
--
--   Illustration
--
--   A, a landholder, knowing of the commission of a murder, within the limits of
--   his commercial property, intentionally misinforms the police that the death
--   has occurred by accident in consequence of the bite of a snake. A is guilty
--   of the offence defined in this section.
--
--   Explanation.-In this section and section 176, "offence" includes any act
--   committed at any place out of Singapore, which if committed in Singapore
--   would be punishable under any of the following sections, namely, 302, 304,
--   382, 392, 393, 394, 395, 396, 397, 399, 402, 435, 436, 449, 450, 459 and
--   460, and "offender" includes any person who is alleged to have been guilty
--   of any such act.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 177; s 40(3)
DECLARE `False Information Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the accused is an individual`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused an individual (a human being)? Paragraph (a) of the punishment applies to an individual; paragraph (b), "in any other case", to a company, association or body of persons (s 11). This leaf chooses the punishment, not whether the offence is made out.
    `legally bound to furnish information on any subject`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused legally bound (s 43) to furnish information on some subject?
    `to any public servant, as such`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the obligation owed to a public servant in that capacity?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `furnishes, as true, information on the subject`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused furnish information on that subject, as true?
    `knows the information to be false`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know the information was false?
    `has reason to believe the information to be false`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused have reason to believe (s 26) the information was false?
    `the information respects the commission of an offence, or is required for the purpose of preventing the commission of an offence, or in order to the apprehension of an offender`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (2) Does the notice or information concern the commission of an offence, or is it required to prevent an offence or to apprehend an offender? By the Explanation to s 177, "offence" here includes an act outside Singapore that would be punishable in Singapore under s 302, 304, 382, 392-397, 399, 402, 435, 436, 449, 450, 459 or 460, and "offender" anyone alleged to have done one. By s 40(3), "offence" also covers another law's offence punishable with 6 months' imprisonment or more.
    `the information`
        IS A STRING @desc The false information, as it is to read in the charge - for example "that the deceased had died by accident in consequence of the bite of a snake"
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 177(1)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 177(1)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "177(1)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 177(1)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 177(1)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "177(1)(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 177(2)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 177(2)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "177(2)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 177(2)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 177(2)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "177(2)(b)"
    words                    IS "fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused, legally bound to furnish information to a public servant, furnishes as true information known or believed to be false, within section 177(1) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `False Information Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `furnishes false information to a public servant` f IF
        "(1) A person who, being"
    AND f's `legally bound to furnish information on any subject`
    AND f's `to any public servant, as such`
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `furnishes, as true, information on the subject`
    AND "which the person"
    AND (    f's `knows the information to be false`
         OR  f's `has reason to believe the information to be false` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 177(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (furnishing false information)
GIVEN f IS A `False Information Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 177(1)` f IF
        "A person who"
    ... `furnishes false information to a public servant` f

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence under section 177(1) of the Penal Code 1871 that section 177(2) punishes more severely (the information respects an offence)
GIVEN f IS A `False Information Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 177(2)` f IF
        "the person who is guilty of an offence under that subsection"
    AND `offence under s 177(1)` f
    AND "(2) If the information which the person is legally bound to furnish"
    AND f's `the information respects the commission of an offence, or is required for the purpose of preventing the commission of an offence, or in order to the apprehension of an offender`

@export Frame a charge under section 177(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (furnishing false information to a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `False Information Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 177(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "177(1)(a)" ELSE "177(1)(b)") "furnishing false information to a public servant"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 177(1)(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 177(1)(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 177(1)` f)
        (CONCAT "being legally bound to furnish information to ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, did furnish, as true, information ", f's `the information`, ", which you ", (IF f's `knows the information to be false` THEN "knew" ELSE "had reason to believe"), " to be false", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound to furnish information on any subject`) "legally bound to furnish information on the subject"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `to any public servant, as such` AND f's `public servant`) "to a public servant, as such"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `furnishes, as true, information on the subject`) "furnishes, as true, information on the subject"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `knows the information to be false` OR f's `has reason to believe the information to be false`) "which the person knows or has reason to believe to be false"),
            (`missing unless` (`furnishes false information to a public servant` f) "the elements of section 177(1) taken together")))

@export Frame a charge under section 177(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (furnishing false information to a public servant respecting an offence), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `False Information Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 177(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "177(2)(a)" ELSE "177(2)(b)") "furnishing false information to a public servant respecting an offence"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 177(2)(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 177(2)(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 177(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "being legally bound to furnish information to ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, did furnish, as true, information ", f's `the information`, ", which you ", (IF f's `knows the information to be false` THEN "knew" ELSE "had reason to believe"), " to be false", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound to furnish information on any subject`) "legally bound to furnish information on the subject"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `to any public servant, as such` AND f's `public servant`) "to a public servant, as such"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `furnishes, as true, information on the subject`) "furnishes, as true, information on the subject"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `knows the information to be false` OR f's `has reason to believe the information to be false`) "which the person knows or has reason to believe to be false"),
            (`missing unless` (`furnishes false information to a public servant` f) "the elements of section 177(1) taken together"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `the information respects the commission of an offence, or is required for the purpose of preventing the commission of an offence, or in order to the apprehension of an offender`) "the information respects the commission of an offence, or is required to prevent one or to apprehend an offender")))

§§ `s 178 - Refusing oath when duly required to take oath by a public servant`

--   178. Whoever refuses to bind himself by an oath to state the truth, when
--   required so to bind himself by a public servant legally competent to require
--   that he shall so bind himself, shall be punished with imprisonment for a
--   term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000,
--   or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 178; s 21(2); s 51
DECLARE `Refusing Oath Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `required to bind himself by an oath to state the truth`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused required to bind themselves by an oath (s 51: including a solemn affirmation) to state the truth?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21, read with section 21(2): for this section a judge as defined in the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016 is NOT a public servant? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21, for sections 175, 178, 179, 180 and 228`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `legally competent to require that he shall so bind himself`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the public servant who required it legally competent to require it?
    `refuses to bind himself by an oath to state the truth`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused refuse to bind themselves by that oath?
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 178
`punishment prescribed by s 178` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "178"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused refuses to take an oath to state the truth when duly required by a public servant, within section 178 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Refusing Oath Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refuses an oath required by a public servant` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `refuses to bind himself by an oath to state the truth`
    AND "when"
    AND f's `required to bind himself by an oath to state the truth`
    AND "by a"
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `legally competent to require that he shall so bind himself`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 178 of the Penal Code 1871 (refusing an oath)
GIVEN f IS A `Refusing Oath Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 178` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `refuses an oath required by a public servant` f

@export Frame a charge under section 178 of the Penal Code 1871 (refusing an oath when duly required by a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Refusing Oath Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 178` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "178" "refusing an oath when duly required by a public servant"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 178`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 178` f)
        (CONCAT "did refuse to bind yourself by an oath to state the truth when required so to bind yourself by ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant legally competent to require that you should so bind yourself", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `refuses to bind himself by an oath to state the truth`) "refuses to bind himself by an oath to state the truth"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `required to bind himself by an oath to state the truth`) "when required so to bind himself"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "by a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally competent to require that he shall so bind himself`) "legally competent to require it"),
            (`missing unless` (`refuses an oath required by a public servant` f) "the elements of section 178 taken together")))

§§ `s 179 - Refusing to answer public servant authorised to question`

--   179. A person who, being legally bound to state the truth on any subject to
--   any public servant, refuses to answer any question demanded of the person
--   touching that subject by that public servant, in the exercise of the legal
--   powers of such public servant, shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 179; s 21(2)
DECLARE `Refusing to Answer Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the accused is an individual`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused an individual (a human being)? Paragraph (a) of the punishment applies to an individual; paragraph (b), "in any other case", to a company, association or body of persons (s 11). This leaf chooses the punishment, not whether the offence is made out.
    `legally bound to state the truth on any subject to any public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused legally bound (s 43) to state the truth on some subject to a public servant?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21, read with section 21(2): for this section a judge as defined in the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016 is NOT a public servant? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21, for sections 175, 178, 179, 180 and 228`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `refuses to answer any question demanded touching that subject`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused refuse to answer a question demanded of them on that subject?
    `demanded by that public servant in the exercise of the legal powers of such public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the question demanded by that public servant in the exercise of the public servant's legal powers?
    `the subject`
        IS A STRING @desc The subject on which the accused was bound to state the truth, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 179(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 179(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "179(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 179(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 179(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "179(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused, legally bound to state the truth to a public servant, refuses to answer a question the public servant lawfully demands, within section 179 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Refusing to Answer Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refuses to answer a public servant` f IF
        "A person who, being"
    AND f's `legally bound to state the truth on any subject to any public servant`
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `refuses to answer any question demanded touching that subject`
    AND f's `demanded by that public servant in the exercise of the legal powers of such public servant`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 179 of the Penal Code 1871 (refusing to answer a public servant authorised to question)
GIVEN f IS A `Refusing to Answer Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 179` f IF
        "A person who"
    ... `refuses to answer a public servant` f

@export Frame a charge under section 179 of the Penal Code 1871 (refusing to answer a public servant authorised to question), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Refusing to Answer Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 179` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "179(a)" ELSE "179(b)") "refusing to answer a public servant authorised to question"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 179(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 179(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 179` f)
        (CONCAT "being legally bound to state the truth on ", f's `the subject`, " to ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, did refuse to answer a question touching that subject demanded of you by the said public servant in the exercise of the legal powers of such public servant", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound to state the truth on any subject to any public servant`) "legally bound to state the truth on the subject"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "to a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `refuses to answer any question demanded touching that subject`) "refuses to answer a question demanded touching that subject"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `demanded by that public servant in the exercise of the legal powers of such public servant`) "demanded by that public servant in the exercise of the public servant's legal powers"),
            (`missing unless` (`refuses to answer a public servant` f) "the elements of section 179 taken together")))

§§ `s 180 - Refusing to sign statement`

--   180. Whoever refuses to sign any statement made by him, when required to
--   sign that statement by a public servant legally competent to require that he
--   shall sign that statement, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 3 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,500, or
--   with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 180; s 21(2)
DECLARE `Refusing to Sign Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `refuses to sign any statement made by him`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused refuse to sign a statement the accused had made?
    `required to sign that statement`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused required to sign it?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21, read with section 21(2): for this section a judge as defined in the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016 is NOT a public servant? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21, for sections 175, 178, 179, 180 and 228`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `legally competent to require that he shall sign that statement`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the public servant who required it legally competent to require it?
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 180
`punishment prescribed by s 180` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "180"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 3
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 2500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused refuses to sign a statement when duly required by a public servant, within section 180 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Refusing to Sign Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refuses to sign a statement` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `refuses to sign any statement made by him`
    AND "when"
    AND f's `required to sign that statement`
    AND "by a"
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `legally competent to require that he shall sign that statement`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 180 of the Penal Code 1871 (refusing to sign a statement)
GIVEN f IS A `Refusing to Sign Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 180` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `refuses to sign a statement` f

@export Frame a charge under section 180 of the Penal Code 1871 (refusing to sign a statement), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Refusing to Sign Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 180` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "180" "refusing to sign a statement"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 180`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 180` f)
        (CONCAT "did refuse to sign a statement made by you, when required to sign that statement by ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant legally competent to require that you should sign it", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `refuses to sign any statement made by him`) "refuses to sign a statement made by him"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `required to sign that statement`) "when required to sign that statement"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "by a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally competent to require that he shall sign that statement`) "legally competent to require it"),
            (`missing unless` (`refuses to sign a statement` f) "the elements of section 180 taken together")))

§§ `s 181 - False statement on oath to public servant or person authorised to administer an oath`

--   181. Whoever, being legally bound by an oath to state the truth on any
--   subject to any public servant or other person authorised by law to
--   administer such oaths, makes to such public servant or other person as
--   aforesaid, touching that subject, any statement which is false, and which he
--   either knows or believes to be false or does not believe to be true, shall
--   be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, and
--   shall also be liable to fine.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 181; s 51
DECLARE `False Statement on Oath Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `legally bound by an oath to state the truth on any subject`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused legally bound by an oath (s 51: including a solemn affirmation) to state the truth on some subject?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `other person authorised by law to administer such oaths`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not to a public servant, was the oath owed to some other person authorised by law to administer such oaths?
    `makes to such public servant or other person, touching that subject, any statement`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make a statement on that subject to that public servant or person?
    `the statement is false`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement false?
    `he knows or believes it to be false`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know or believe it to be false?
    `he does not believe it to be true`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused not believe it to be true?
    `the person to whom it was made`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant or other person to whom the statement was made, as the charge names them
    `the statement`
        IS A STRING @desc The false statement, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 181
`punishment prescribed by s 181` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "181"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused, bound by oath to state the truth to a public servant or a person authorised to administer oaths, makes a false statement, within section 181 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `False Statement on Oath Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `makes a false statement on oath` f IF
        "Whoever, being"
    AND f's `legally bound by an oath to state the truth on any subject`
    AND "to any"
    AND (    f's `public servant`
         OR  f's `other person authorised by law to administer such oaths` )
    AND f's `makes to such public servant or other person, touching that subject, any statement`
    AND "which is"
    AND f's `the statement is false`
    AND "and which he either"
    AND (    f's `he knows or believes it to be false`
         OR  f's `he does not believe it to be true` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 181 of the Penal Code 1871 (false statement on oath to a public servant)
GIVEN f IS A `False Statement on Oath Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 181` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `makes a false statement on oath` f

@export Frame a charge under section 181 of the Penal Code 1871 (false statement on oath to a public servant or a person authorised to administer an oath), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `False Statement on Oath Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 181` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "181" "false statement on oath to a public servant or a person authorised to administer an oath"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 181`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 181` f)
        (CONCAT "being legally bound by an oath to state the truth, did make to ", `one person` (f's `the person to whom it was made`), ", a statement ", f's `the statement`, ", which was false and which you ", (IF f's `he knows or believes it to be false` THEN "knew or believed to be false" ELSE "did not believe to be true"), `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound by an oath to state the truth on any subject`) "legally bound by an oath to state the truth on the subject"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant` OR f's `other person authorised by law to administer such oaths`) "to a public servant or other person authorised by law to administer such oaths"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `makes to such public servant or other person, touching that subject, any statement`) "makes a statement touching that subject"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `the statement is false`) "which is false"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `he knows or believes it to be false` OR f's `he does not believe it to be true`) "which he knows or believes to be false or does not believe to be true"),
            (`missing unless` (`makes a false statement on oath` f) "the elements of section 181 taken together")))

§§ `s 182 - False information, with intent to cause a public servant to use his lawful power to the injury of another person`

--   182. Whoever gives to any public servant any information which he knows or
--   believes to be false, intending thereby to cause, or knowing it to be likely
--   that he will thereby cause, such public servant to use the lawful power of
--   such public servant to the injury or annoyance of any person, or to do or
--   omit anything which such public servant ought not to, or would not, do or
--   omit if the true state of facts respecting which such information is given
--   were known by him, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--   extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
--
--   Illustrations
--
--   (a) A informs a superintendent of police that Z, a police officer
--   subordinate to such superintendent, has been guilty of neglect of duty or
--   misconduct, knowing such information to be false, and knowing it to be
--   likely that the information will cause the superintendent to dismiss Z. A
--   has committed the offence defined in this section.
--
--   (b) A falsely informs a public servant that Z has contraband opium in a
--   secret place, knowing such information to be false, and knowing that it is
--   likely that the consequence of the information will be a search of Z's
--   premises, attended with annoyance to Z. A has committed the offence defined
--   in this section.
--
--   (c) A falsely informs a policeman that he has been assaulted and robbed by a
--   person whose identity he does not know. A also mentions that he often sees
--   that person going in and out of a block of flats, knowing it to be likely
--   that in consequence of this information, the police will make inquiries and
--   institute searches in the block of flats to the annoyance of the flat
--   dwellers or some of them. A has committed an offence under this section.
--
--   (d) A informs a policeman that A does not know the identity of the suspect
--   of a criminal offence, knowing such information to be false, and knowing it
--   to be likely that in consequence of this information, the policeman will
--   expend additional time and resources to identify the suspect which will not
--   be so expended if A had informed the policeman that A knew the identity of
--   the suspect. A has committed an offence under this section.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 182; s 44
DECLARE `False Information to Public Servant Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `gives to any public servant any information`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused give information to a public servant?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `he knows the information to be false`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know the information was false?
    `he believes the information to be false`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused believe the information was false?
    `intending thereby to cause`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend by it to cause the result below?
    `knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know it was likely that the information would cause the result below?
    `such public servant to use the lawful power of such public servant to the injury or annoyance of any person`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Result (i): the public servant using the public servant's lawful power to the injury (s 44) or annoyance of anyone - for example a search of someone's premises, or inquiries in a block of flats?
    `such public servant to do or omit anything which such public servant ought not to, or would not, do or omit if the true state of facts were known by him`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Result (ii): the public servant doing or omitting anything the public servant ought not to, or would not, do or omit if the true facts were known - for example spending time and resources that would not otherwise be spent?
    `the information`
        IS A STRING @desc The false information, as it is to read in the charge - for example "that you had been robbed of your handphone by an unknown person"
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 182
`punishment prescribed by s 182` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "182"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused gives a public servant false information intending or knowing it likely to cause the public servant to use lawful power to someone's injury or annoyance, or to act as the public servant would not on the true facts, within section 182 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `False Information to Public Servant Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `gives false information to a public servant` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `gives to any public servant any information`
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND "which he"
    AND (    f's `he knows the information to be false`
         OR  f's `he believes the information to be false` )
    AND (    f's `intending thereby to cause`
         OR  f's `knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause` )
    AND (    f's `such public servant to use the lawful power of such public servant to the injury or annoyance of any person`
         OR  f's `such public servant to do or omit anything which such public servant ought not to, or would not, do or omit if the true state of facts were known by him` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 182 of the Penal Code 1871 (false information, with intent to cause a public servant to use lawful power to the injury of another)
GIVEN f IS A `False Information to Public Servant Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 182` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `gives false information to a public servant` f

@export Frame a charge under section 182 of the Penal Code 1871 (giving false information to a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `False Information to Public Servant Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 182` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "182" "giving false information to a public servant"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 182`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 182` f)
        (CONCAT "did give to ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, information ", f's `the information`, ", which you ", (IF f's `he knows the information to be false` THEN "knew" ELSE "believed"), " to be false, ", (IF f's `intending thereby to cause` THEN "intending thereby to cause" ELSE "knowing it to be likely that you would thereby cause"), " the said public servant to ", `joined with` ", or to " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's `such public servant to use the lawful power of such public servant to the injury or annoyance of any person`) "use the lawful power of such public servant to the injury or annoyance of any person"), (`included if` (f's `such public servant to do or omit anything which such public servant ought not to, or would not, do or omit if the true state of facts were known by him`) "do or omit anything which such public servant ought not to, or would not, do or omit if the true state of facts respecting which such information was given were known by him"))), `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `gives to any public servant any information` AND f's `public servant`) "gives to a public servant any information"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `he knows the information to be false` OR f's `he believes the information to be false`) "which he knows or believes to be false"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `intending thereby to cause` OR f's `knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause`) "intending thereby to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `such public servant to use the lawful power of such public servant to the injury or annoyance of any person` OR f's `such public servant to do or omit anything which such public servant ought not to, or would not, do or omit if the true state of facts were known by him`) "such public servant to use lawful power to the injury or annoyance of any person, or to do or omit anything he would not on the true facts"),
            (`missing unless` (`gives false information to a public servant` f) "the elements of section 182 taken together")))

§§ `s 183 - Resistance to taking of property by lawful authority of public servant`

--   183. A person who offers any resistance to the taking of any property by the
--   lawful authority of any public servant, knowing or having reason to believe
--   that the person is such public servant, shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 183
DECLARE `Resisting Taking of Property Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the accused is an individual`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused an individual (a human being)? Paragraph (a) of the punishment applies to an individual; paragraph (b), "in any other case", to a company, association or body of persons (s 11). This leaf chooses the punishment, not whether the offence is made out.
    `offers any resistance to the taking of any property`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused offer any resistance to the taking of property?
    `by the lawful authority of any public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the property being taken by the lawful authority of a public servant?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `knowing that the person is such public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know that the person was such a public servant?
    `having reason to believe that the person is such public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused have reason to believe (s 26) that the person was such a public servant?
    `the property`
        IS A STRING @desc The property, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 183(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 183(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "183(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 183(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 183(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "183(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused resists the taking of property by the lawful authority of a public servant, within section 183 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Resisting Taking of Property Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `resists the taking of property by a public servant` f IF
        "A person who"
    AND f's `offers any resistance to the taking of any property`
    AND f's `by the lawful authority of any public servant`
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND (    f's `knowing that the person is such public servant`
         OR  f's `having reason to believe that the person is such public servant` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 183 of the Penal Code 1871 (resistance to the taking of property by the lawful authority of a public servant)
GIVEN f IS A `Resisting Taking of Property Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 183` f IF
        "A person who"
    ... `resists the taking of property by a public servant` f

@export Frame a charge under section 183 of the Penal Code 1871 (resistance to the taking of property by the lawful authority of a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Resisting Taking of Property Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 183` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "183(a)" ELSE "183(b)") "resistance to the taking of property by the lawful authority of a public servant"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 183(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 183(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 183` f)
        (CONCAT "did offer resistance to the taking of ", f's `the property`, " by the lawful authority of ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, ", (IF f's `knowing that the person is such public servant` THEN "knowing" ELSE "having reason to believe"), " that the said person was such public servant", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `offers any resistance to the taking of any property`) "offers resistance to the taking of property"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `by the lawful authority of any public servant` AND f's `public servant`) "by the lawful authority of a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `knowing that the person is such public servant` OR f's `having reason to believe that the person is such public servant`) "knowing or having reason to believe that the person is such public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (`resists the taking of property by a public servant` f) "the elements of section 183 taken together")))

§§ `s 184 - Obstructing sale of property offered for sale by authority of public servant`

--   184. A person who intentionally obstructs any sale of property offered for
--   sale by the lawful authority of any public servant as such, shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 184
DECLARE `Obstructing Sale Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the accused is an individual`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused an individual (a human being)? Paragraph (a) of the punishment applies to an individual; paragraph (b), "in any other case", to a company, association or body of persons (s 11). This leaf chooses the punishment, not whether the offence is made out.
    intentionally
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act intentionally (s 26C)?
    `obstructs any sale of property`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused obstruct a sale of property?
    `offered for sale by the lawful authority of any public servant as such`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the property offered for sale by the lawful authority of a public servant as such?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `the property`
        IS A STRING @desc The property, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 184(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 184(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "184(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 1
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 184(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 184(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "184(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused intentionally obstructs a sale of property offered by the lawful authority of a public servant, within section 184 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS AN `Obstructing Sale Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `obstructs a sale by a public servant` f IF
        "A person who"
    AND f's intentionally
    AND f's `obstructs any sale of property`
    AND f's `offered for sale by the lawful authority of any public servant as such`
    AND f's `public servant`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 184 of the Penal Code 1871 (obstructing a sale of property offered by the authority of a public servant)
GIVEN f IS AN `Obstructing Sale Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 184` f IF
        "A person who"
    ... `obstructs a sale by a public servant` f

@export Frame a charge under section 184 of the Penal Code 1871 (obstructing a sale of property offered for sale by the authority of a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Obstructing Sale Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 184` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "184(a)" ELSE "184(b)") "obstructing a sale of property offered for sale by the authority of a public servant"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 184(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 184(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 184` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally obstruct the sale of ", f's `the property`, ", offered for sale by the lawful authority of ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `obstructs any sale of property`) "obstructs a sale of property"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `offered for sale by the lawful authority of any public servant as such` AND f's `public servant`) "offered for sale by the lawful authority of a public servant as such"),
            (`missing unless` (`obstructs a sale by a public servant` f) "the elements of section 184 taken together")))

§§ `s 185 - Illegal purchase or bid for property offered for sale by authority of public servant`

--   185. A person who, at any sale of property held by the lawful authority of a
--   public servant as such, purchases or bids for any property on account of the
--   person or another person, whom the person knows to be under a legal
--   incapacity to purchase that property at that sale, or bids for such property
--   not intending to perform the obligations under which the person lays himself
--   by such bidding, shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 185
DECLARE `Illegal Bid Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the accused is an individual`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused an individual (a human being)? Paragraph (a) of the punishment applies to an individual; paragraph (b), "in any other case", to a company, association or body of persons (s 11). This leaf chooses the punishment, not whether the offence is made out.
    `at any sale of property held by the lawful authority of a public servant as such`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it at a sale of property held by the lawful authority of a public servant as such?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `purchases or bids for any property on account of the person or another person`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused purchase or bid for property on their own account or another's?
    `whom the person knows to be under a legal incapacity to purchase that property at that sale`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know that the person on whose account they bought or bid was under a legal incapacity to purchase that property at that sale?
    `bids for such property not intending to perform the obligations under which the person lays himself by such bidding`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused bid without intending to perform the obligations the bid created?
    `the property`
        IS A STRING @desc The property, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 185(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 185(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "185(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 1
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 185(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 185(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "185(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused makes an illegal purchase or bid at a sale held by the authority of a public servant, within section 185 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS AN `Illegal Bid Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `makes an illegal purchase or bid at a sale by a public servant` f IF
        "A person who"
    AND f's `at any sale of property held by the lawful authority of a public servant as such`
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND (    (    f's `purchases or bids for any property on account of the person or another person`
              AND f's `whom the person knows to be under a legal incapacity to purchase that property at that sale` )
         OR  f's `bids for such property not intending to perform the obligations under which the person lays himself by such bidding` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 185 of the Penal Code 1871 (illegal purchase or bid at a sale by the authority of a public servant)
GIVEN f IS AN `Illegal Bid Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 185` f IF
        "A person who"
    ... `makes an illegal purchase or bid at a sale by a public servant` f

@export Frame a charge under section 185 of the Penal Code 1871 (illegal purchase or bid for property offered for sale by the authority of a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Illegal Bid Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 185` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "185(a)" ELSE "185(b)") "illegal purchase or bid for property offered for sale by the authority of a public servant"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 185(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 185(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 185` f)
        (CONCAT "at a sale of property held by the lawful authority of ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, did ", (IF f's `bids for such property not intending to perform the obligations under which the person lays himself by such bidding` THEN "bid for " ELSE "purchase or bid for "), f's `the property`, (IF f's `bids for such property not intending to perform the obligations under which the person lays himself by such bidding` THEN ", not intending to perform the obligations under which you laid yourself by such bidding" ELSE ", on account of a person whom you knew to be under a legal incapacity to purchase that property at that sale"), `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `at any sale of property held by the lawful authority of a public servant as such` AND f's `public servant`) "at a sale of property held by the lawful authority of a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` ((f's `purchases or bids for any property on account of the person or another person` AND f's `whom the person knows to be under a legal incapacity to purchase that property at that sale`) OR f's `bids for such property not intending to perform the obligations under which the person lays himself by such bidding`) "purchases or bids on account of a person known to be under a legal incapacity to purchase, or bids not intending to perform the obligations of the bid"),
            (`missing unless` (`makes an illegal purchase or bid at a sale by a public servant` f) "the elements of section 185 taken together")))

§§ `s 186 - Obstructing public servant in discharge of his public functions`

--   186.-(1) A person who voluntarily obstructs any public servant in the
--   discharge of the public servant's public functions, shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,500, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.
--
--   (2) For the purposes of this section, an obstruction may be caused other
--   than by the use of physical means or threatening language by a person
--   against a public servant.
--
--   Illustration
--
--   A group of paramedics from the Singapore Civil Defence Force intends to take
--   the lift to the 30th storey of a block of flats to reach a person suffering
--   from a heart attack. A decides to play a prank on the paramedics by telling
--   them that the lift has broken down, knowing this to be false. The paramedics
--   took the stairs because of what A told them and reached the person 15
--   minutes later than if they had taken the lift. A has voluntarily obstructed
--   the paramedics in the discharge of their public function.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 186
DECLARE `Obstructing Public Servant Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the accused is an individual`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused an individual (a human being)? Paragraph (a) of the punishment applies to an individual; paragraph (b), "in any other case", to a company, association or body of persons (s 11). This leaf chooses the punishment, not whether the offence is made out.
    voluntarily
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause the obstruction voluntarily - by means the accused intended, or knew or had reason to believe likely to cause it (s 26A)?
    obstructs
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused obstruct the public servant? By s 186(2) an obstruction need not be by physical means or threatening language - a false report that sends paramedics up the stairs is one (s 186 illustration).
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `in the discharge of the public servant's public functions`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the public servant discharging the public servant's public functions at the time?
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 186(1)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 186(1)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "186(1)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 2500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 186(1)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 186(1)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "186(1)(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

-- s 186(2) widens `obstructs` (see its @desc); it adds no limb.
@export Whether the accused voluntarily obstructs a public servant in the discharge of the public servant's public functions, within section 186 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS AN `Obstructing Public Servant Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `voluntarily obstructs a public servant` f IF
        "(1) A person who"
    AND f's voluntarily
    AND f's obstructs
    AND "any"
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `in the discharge of the public servant's public functions`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 186(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (obstructing a public servant in the discharge of public functions)
GIVEN f IS AN `Obstructing Public Servant Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 186` f IF
        "A person who"
    ... `voluntarily obstructs a public servant` f

@export Frame a charge under section 186 of the Penal Code 1871 (obstructing a public servant in the discharge of public functions), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Obstructing Public Servant Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 186` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "186(1)(a)" ELSE "186(1)(b)") "obstructing a public servant in the discharge of public functions"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 186(1)(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 186(1)(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 186` f)
        (CONCAT "did voluntarily obstruct ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, in the discharge of ", `possessive pronoun` (f's `the public servant`'s pronoun), " public functions", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's voluntarily) "voluntarily"),
            (`missing unless` (f's obstructs) "obstructs"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `in the discharge of the public servant's public functions`) "in the discharge of the public servant's public functions"),
            (`missing unless` (`voluntarily obstructs a public servant` f) "the elements of section 186 taken together")))

§§ `s 187 - Omission to assist public servant when bound by law to give assistance`

--   187.-(1) A person who, being bound by law to render or furnish assistance to
--   any public servant in the execution of the public servant's public duty,
--   intentionally omits to give such assistance, shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.
--
--   (2) If such assistance is demanded of the person mentioned in subsection (1)
--   by a public servant legally competent to make such demand for the purposes
--   of executing any process lawfully issued by a court, or of preventing the
--   commission of an offence, or of suppressing a riot or an affray, or of
--   apprehending a person charged with or guilty of an offence, or of having
--   escaped from lawful custody, the person who is guilty of an offence under
--   that subsection shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 187
DECLARE `Omission to Assist Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the accused is an individual`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused an individual (a human being)? Paragraph (a) of the punishment applies to an individual; paragraph (b), "in any other case", to a company, association or body of persons (s 11). This leaf chooses the punishment, not whether the offence is made out.
    `bound by law to render or furnish assistance to any public servant in the execution of the public servant's public duty`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused bound by law to render or furnish assistance to a public servant executing the public servant's public duty?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    intentionally
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act intentionally (s 26C)?
    `omits to give such assistance`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused fail to give that assistance?
    `demanded by a public servant legally competent to make such demand`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (2) Was the assistance demanded by a public servant legally competent to demand it?
    `for the purposes of executing any process lawfully issued by a court`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (2) ... for executing process lawfully issued by a court?
    `of preventing the commission of an offence`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (2) ... for preventing the commission of an offence?
    `of suppressing a riot or an affray`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (2) ... for suppressing a riot or an affray?
    `of apprehending a person charged with or guilty of an offence, or of having escaped from lawful custody`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (2) ... for apprehending a person charged with or guilty of an offence, or of having escaped from lawful custody?
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 187(1)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 187(1)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "187(1)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 1
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 187(1)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 187(1)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "187(1)(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 187(2)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 187(2)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "187(2)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 187(2)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 187(2)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "187(2)(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused, bound by law to assist a public servant, intentionally omits to, within section 187(1) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Assist Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `omits to assist a public servant` f IF
        "(1) A person who, being"
    AND f's `bound by law to render or furnish assistance to any public servant in the execution of the public servant's public duty`
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's intentionally
    AND f's `omits to give such assistance`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 187(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (omission to assist a public servant)
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Assist Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 187(1)` f IF
        "A person who"
    ... `omits to assist a public servant` f

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence under section 187(1) of the Penal Code 1871 that section 187(2) punishes more severely (assistance demanded to execute process, prevent an offence, suppress a riot or apprehend an offender)
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Assist Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 187(2)` f IF
        "the person who is guilty of an offence under that subsection"
    AND `offence under s 187(1)` f
    AND "(2) If such assistance is"
    AND f's `demanded by a public servant legally competent to make such demand`
    AND (    f's `for the purposes of executing any process lawfully issued by a court`
         OR  f's `of preventing the commission of an offence`
         OR  f's `of suppressing a riot or an affray`
         OR  f's `of apprehending a person charged with or guilty of an offence, or of having escaped from lawful custody` )

@export Frame a charge under section 187(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (omission to assist a public servant when bound by law to give assistance), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Assist Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 187(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "187(1)(a)" ELSE "187(1)(b)") "omission to assist a public servant when bound by law to give assistance"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 187(1)(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 187(1)(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 187(1)` f)
        (CONCAT "being bound by law to render assistance to ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, in the execution of ", `possessive pronoun` (f's `the public servant`'s pronoun), " public duty, did intentionally omit to give such assistance", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `bound by law to render or furnish assistance to any public servant in the execution of the public servant's public duty` AND f's `public servant`) "bound by law to render or furnish assistance to a public servant in the execution of the public servant's public duty"),
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `omits to give such assistance`) "omits to give such assistance"),
            (`missing unless` (`omits to assist a public servant` f) "the elements of section 187(1) taken together")))

@export Frame a charge under section 187(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (omission to assist a public servant when demanded for the execution of process or the prevention of an offence), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Omission to Assist Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 187(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "187(2)(a)" ELSE "187(2)(b)") "omission to assist a public servant when demanded for the execution of process or the prevention of an offence"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 187(2)(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 187(2)(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 187(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "being bound by law to render assistance to ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, in the execution of ", `possessive pronoun` (f's `the public servant`'s pronoun), " public duty, did intentionally omit to give such assistance", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `bound by law to render or furnish assistance to any public servant in the execution of the public servant's public duty` AND f's `public servant`) "bound by law to render or furnish assistance to a public servant in the execution of the public servant's public duty"),
            (`missing unless` (f's intentionally) "intentionally"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `omits to give such assistance`) "omits to give such assistance"),
            (`missing unless` (`omits to assist a public servant` f) "the elements of section 187(1) taken together"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `demanded by a public servant legally competent to make such demand`) "demanded by a public servant legally competent to make such demand"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `for the purposes of executing any process lawfully issued by a court` OR f's `of preventing the commission of an offence` OR f's `of suppressing a riot or an affray` OR f's `of apprehending a person charged with or guilty of an offence, or of having escaped from lawful custody`) "for executing process lawfully issued by a court, preventing an offence, suppressing a riot or an affray, or apprehending an offender or escapee")))

§§ `s 188 - Disobedience to order duly promulgated by public servant`

--   188.-(1) A person who, knowing that by an order promulgated by a public
--   servant lawfully empowered to promulgate such order the person is directed
--   to abstain from a certain act, or to take certain order with certain
--   property in the person's possession or under the person's management,
--   disobeys such direction, shall, if such disobedience causes or tends to
--   cause obstruction, annoyance or injury, or risk of obstruction, annoyance or
--   injury, to any person lawfully employed -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.
--
--   (2) If such disobedience mentioned in subsection (1) causes or tends to
--   cause danger to human life, health or safety, or causes or tends to cause a
--   riot or an affray, the person who is guilty of an offence under that
--   subsection shall -
--
--   (a) in the case of an individual, be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or
--   with both; or
--
--   (b) in any other case, be punished with fine which may extend to $10,000.
--
--   Explanation.-It is not necessary that the offender should intend to produce
--   harm, or contemplate his disobedience as likely to produce harm. It is
--   sufficient that he knows of the order which he disobeys, and that his
--   disobedience produces, or is likely to produce, harm.
--
--   Illustration
--
--   An order is promulgated by a public servant lawfully empowered to promulgate
--   such order, directing that a religious procession must not pass down a
--   certain street. A knowingly disobeys the order, and thereby causes danger of
--   riot. A has committed the offence defined in this section.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 188
DECLARE `Disobedience to Order Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the accused is an individual`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused an individual (a human being)? Paragraph (a) of the punishment applies to an individual; paragraph (b), "in any other case", to a company, association or body of persons (s 11). This leaf chooses the punishment, not whether the offence is made out.
    `knowing that by an order promulgated by a public servant he is directed`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know of the order and that it directed the accused? The Explanation: that knowledge is enough - the accused need not intend or contemplate harm.
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `lawfully empowered to promulgate such order`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the public servant lawfully empowered to promulgate the order?
    `directed to abstain from a certain act`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the order direct the accused to abstain from a certain act?
    `directed to take certain order with certain property in the person's possession or under the person's management`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the order direct the accused to take certain order with property in the accused's possession or under the accused's management?
    `disobeys such direction`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused disobey the direction?
    `causes or tends to cause obstruction, annoyance or injury, or risk of obstruction, annoyance or injury, to any person lawfully employed`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (1) Did the disobedience cause, or tend to cause, obstruction, annoyance or injury (s 44), or a risk of it, to any person lawfully employed?
    `causes or tends to cause danger to human life, health or safety, or causes or tends to cause a riot or an affray`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc (2) Did the disobedience cause, or tend to cause, danger to human life, health or safety, or a riot or an affray?
    `the order`
        IS A STRING @desc The order, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 188(1)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 188(1)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "188(1)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one month, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 1
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 188(1)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 188(1)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "188(1)(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 188(2)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 188(2)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "188(2)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 188(2)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 188(2)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "188(2)(b)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $10,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

-- FORK SP-188 (notes/state-public-forks.md): subsection (2) is read as its own harm
-- condition, not as (1)'s harm plus more - so the harm is not in this predicate.
@export Whether the accused, knowing of an order duly promulgated by a public servant, disobeys it, within section 188 of the Penal Code 1871 (before the harm that subsections (1) and (2) each require)
GIVEN f IS A `Disobedience to Order Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `disobeys an order duly promulgated by a public servant` f IF
        "A person who"
    AND f's `knowing that by an order promulgated by a public servant he is directed`
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `lawfully empowered to promulgate such order`
    AND (    f's `directed to abstain from a certain act`
         OR  f's `directed to take certain order with certain property in the person's possession or under the person's management` )
    AND f's `disobeys such direction`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 188(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (disobedience to an order duly promulgated by a public servant)
GIVEN f IS A `Disobedience to Order Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 188(1)` f IF
        `disobeys an order duly promulgated by a public servant` f
    AND "shall, if such disobedience"
    AND f's `causes or tends to cause obstruction, annoyance or injury, or risk of obstruction, annoyance or injury, to any person lawfully employed`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 188(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (disobedience to an order that endangers life, health or safety, or tends to a riot or affray)
GIVEN f IS A `Disobedience to Order Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 188(2)` f IF
        `disobeys an order duly promulgated by a public servant` f
    AND "(2) If such disobedience mentioned in subsection (1)"
    AND f's `causes or tends to cause danger to human life, health or safety, or causes or tends to cause a riot or an affray`

@export Frame a charge under section 188(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (disobedience to an order duly promulgated by a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Disobedience to Order Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 188(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "188(1)(a)" ELSE "188(1)(b)") "disobedience to an order duly promulgated by a public servant"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 188(1)(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 188(1)(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 188(1)` f)
        (CONCAT "knowing that by ", f's `the order`, ", promulgated by ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant lawfully empowered to promulgate such order, you were directed ", (IF f's `directed to abstain from a certain act` THEN "to abstain from a certain act" ELSE "to take certain order with certain property in your possession or under your management"), ", did disobey such direction, and such disobedience ", "caused or tended to cause obstruction, annoyance or injury, or risk of obstruction, annoyance or injury, to persons lawfully employed", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `knowing that by an order promulgated by a public servant he is directed`) "knowing that by an order promulgated by a public servant he is directed"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant` AND f's `lawfully empowered to promulgate such order`) "by a public servant lawfully empowered to promulgate such order"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `directed to abstain from a certain act` OR f's `directed to take certain order with certain property in the person's possession or under the person's management`) "directed to abstain from a certain act, or to take certain order with certain property"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `disobeys such direction`) "disobeys such direction"),
            (`missing unless` (`disobeys an order duly promulgated by a public servant` f) "the elements of section 188 taken together"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `causes or tends to cause obstruction, annoyance or injury, or risk of obstruction, annoyance or injury, to any person lawfully employed`) "such disobedience causes or tends to cause obstruction, annoyance or injury, or risk of it, to any person lawfully employed")))

@export Frame a charge under section 188(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (disobedience to an order duly promulgated by a public servant, causing danger to human life, health or safety, or a riot or affray), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Disobedience to Order Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 188(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN "188(2)(a)" ELSE "188(2)(b)") "disobedience to an order duly promulgated by a public servant, causing danger to human life, health or safety, or a riot or affray"
        (IF f's `the accused is an individual` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 188(2)(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 188(2)(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 188(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "knowing that by ", f's `the order`, ", promulgated by ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant lawfully empowered to promulgate such order, you were directed ", (IF f's `directed to abstain from a certain act` THEN "to abstain from a certain act" ELSE "to take certain order with certain property in your possession or under your management"), ", did disobey such direction, and such disobedience ", "caused or tended to cause danger to human life, health or safety, or a riot or an affray", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `knowing that by an order promulgated by a public servant he is directed`) "knowing that by an order promulgated by a public servant he is directed"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant` AND f's `lawfully empowered to promulgate such order`) "by a public servant lawfully empowered to promulgate such order"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `directed to abstain from a certain act` OR f's `directed to take certain order with certain property in the person's possession or under the person's management`) "directed to abstain from a certain act, or to take certain order with certain property"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `disobeys such direction`) "disobeys such direction"),
            (`missing unless` (`disobeys an order duly promulgated by a public servant` f) "the elements of section 188 taken together"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `causes or tends to cause danger to human life, health or safety, or causes or tends to cause a riot or an affray`) "such disobedience causes or tends to cause danger to human life, health or safety, or a riot or an affray")))

§§ `s 189 - Threat of injury to a public servant`

--   189. Whoever holds out any threat of injury to any public servant, or to any
--   person in whom he believes that public servant to be interested, for the
--   purpose of inducing that public servant to do any act, or to forbear or
--   delay to do any act, connected with the exercise of the public functions of
--   such public servant, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which
--   may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 189; s 44
DECLARE `Threat to Public Servant Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `holds out any threat of injury`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused hold out a threat of injury - any harm illegally caused to body, mind, reputation or property (s 44)?
    `to any public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the threat to the public servant?
    `to any person in whom he believes that public servant to be interested`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the threat to a person in whom the accused believed the public servant to be interested?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    `for the purpose of inducing that public servant to do any act, or to forbear or delay to do any act, connected with the exercise of the public functions of such public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose to induce the public servant to do, or to forbear or delay doing, an act connected with the exercise of the public servant's public functions?
    `the threat`
        IS A STRING @desc The threat, as it is to read in the charge - for example "that you would kill him"
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 189
`punishment prescribed by s 189` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "189"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused threatens injury to a public servant, or to someone in whom the public servant is believed interested, to induce an act or forbearance connected with public functions, within section 189 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Threat to Public Servant Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `threatens a public servant` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `holds out any threat of injury`
    AND (    f's `to any public servant`
         OR  f's `to any person in whom he believes that public servant to be interested` )
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `for the purpose of inducing that public servant to do any act, or to forbear or delay to do any act, connected with the exercise of the public functions of such public servant`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 189 of the Penal Code 1871 (threat of injury to a public servant)
GIVEN f IS A `Threat to Public Servant Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 189` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `threatens a public servant` f

@export Frame a charge under section 189 of the Penal Code 1871 (threat of injury to a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Threat to Public Servant Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 189` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "189" "threat of injury to a public servant"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 189`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 189` f)
        (CONCAT "did hold out a threat of injury ", f's `the threat`, " to ", (IF f's `to any public servant` THEN "" ELSE "a person in whom you believed "), `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant", (IF f's `to any public servant` THEN "" ELSE ", to be interested"), ", for the purpose of inducing the said public servant to do, or to forbear or delay to do, an act connected with the exercise of ", `possessive pronoun` (f's `the public servant`'s pronoun), " public functions", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `holds out any threat of injury`) "holds out a threat of injury"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `to any public servant` OR f's `to any person in whom he believes that public servant to be interested`) "to a public servant, or to a person in whom he believes that public servant to be interested"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `for the purpose of inducing that public servant to do any act, or to forbear or delay to do any act, connected with the exercise of the public functions of such public servant`) "for the purpose of inducing that public servant to do, forbear or delay an act connected with the public servant's public functions"),
            (`missing unless` (`threatens a public servant` f) "the elements of section 189 taken together")))

§§ `s 190 - Threat of injury to induce any person to refrain from applying for protection to a public servant`

--   190. Whoever holds out any threat of injury to any person for the purpose of
--   inducing that person to refrain or desist from making a legal application,
--   for protection against any injury, to any public servant legally empowered
--   as such to give such protection or to cause such protection to be given,
--   shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year,
--   or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 190; s 44
DECLARE `Threat to Deter Protection Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `holds out any threat of injury to any person`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused hold out a threat of injury (s 44) to anyone?
    `for the purpose of inducing that person to refrain or desist from making a legal application for protection against any injury`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose to induce that person to refrain or desist from making a legal application for protection against injury?
    `to any public servant legally empowered as such to give such protection or to cause such protection to be given`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the application one to a public servant legally empowered, as such, to give or cause that protection?
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the person threatened`
        IS A Person @desc The person threatened, as the charge names them
    `the threat`
        IS A STRING @desc The threat, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 190
`punishment prescribed by s 190` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "190"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused threatens injury to induce someone not to apply to a public servant for protection, within section 190 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Threat to Deter Protection Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `threatens a person to deter an application for protection` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `holds out any threat of injury to any person`
    AND f's `for the purpose of inducing that person to refrain or desist from making a legal application for protection against any injury`
    AND f's `to any public servant legally empowered as such to give such protection or to cause such protection to be given`
    AND f's `public servant`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 190 of the Penal Code 1871 (threat of injury to induce a person to refrain from applying for protection to a public servant)
GIVEN f IS A `Threat to Deter Protection Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 190` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `threatens a person to deter an application for protection` f

@export Frame a charge under section 190 of the Penal Code 1871 (threat of injury to induce a person to refrain from applying for protection to a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Threat to Deter Protection Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 190` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "190" "threat of injury to induce a person to refrain from applying for protection to a public servant"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 190`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 190` f)
        (CONCAT "did hold out a threat of injury ", f's `the threat`, " to ", `one person` (f's `the person threatened`), ", for the purpose of inducing ", `object pronoun` (f's `the person threatened`'s pronoun), " to refrain from making a legal application for protection against injury to a public servant legally empowered as such to give such protection", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `holds out any threat of injury to any person`) "holds out a threat of injury to any person"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `for the purpose of inducing that person to refrain or desist from making a legal application for protection against any injury`) "for the purpose of inducing that person to refrain or desist from a legal application for protection"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `to any public servant legally empowered as such to give such protection or to cause such protection to be given` AND f's `public servant`) "to a public servant legally empowered as such to give such protection"),
            (`missing unless` (`threatens a person to deter an application for protection` f) "the elements of section 190 taken together")))
